{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הכושית", :translit "ha-kushit", :gloss "the Cushite woman"} {:he "יפת מראה", :translit "yefat mar'eh", :gloss "beautiful of appearance"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "הכושית", :b "יפת מראה"}], :frame {:text "The Torah calls Miriam 'the Cushite woman.' The Midrash explains this as a euphemism: just as everyone agrees a Cushite is distinct in skin, so everyone agreed Miriam was distinct in beauty and righteous deeds (Sifrei Zuta 12:1, Moed Katan 16b). The Ba'al HaTurim compresses this tradition into a gematria equating 'the Cushite woman' with 'beautiful in appearance.'", :sources ["Sifrei Zuta 12:1" "Moed Katan 16b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "הכושית", :a-value 741, :b "יפת מראה", :b-value 736, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:30.412457972Z", :model "glm-5.2"}